# Line endings: most sources are stored with LF. The MiSTer framework (sys/)
# and a few template files carry CRLF as the template ships them, so there is
# no blanket "* text=auto" (it would renormalize those blobs); only the types
# below are pinned.

# Shell scripts must stay LF: they also run on the MiSTer (Linux). (clean.bat
# is stored as the template ships it.)
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch line endings, no textual diffs.
*.rbf  binary
*.rom  binary
*.nvr  binary
*.bin  binary
*.sof  binary
*.mif  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
releases/MiSTer binary
